AI Contribution Log

Project: BFS vs DFS Performance Comparison

1. Purpose of Using AI

AI was used as a learning and coding-support tool to understand the assignment, prepare the program structure, explain the algorithms, and improve the documentation. The generated code was reviewed and tested by the student.

2. AI Contribution Details

Sr. No.          AI Assistance Used                         Student Action

1                Explained the difference between            Understood that BFS uses a queue and DFS uses a stack.
                 BFS and DFS.

2                Suggested a binary-tree graph               Understood the graph structure and selected a search target.
                 for testing.

3                Helped prepare the BFS implementation.      Reviewed the code and understood queue operations.

4                Helped prepare the DFS implementation.      Reviewed the code and understood stack operations.

5                Suggested measuring performance             Ran the program and observed execution time and node count.
                 through repeated runs. 

6                Helped prepare the report and README.       Reviewed and edited the documentation.

3. Student Responsibility

I reviewed the AI-generated suggestions, understood the main logic, checked the program output, and organized the files for GitHub and Moodle submission.

4. Learning Outcome

Through this activity, I learned:

How BFS and DFS algorithms work.

How queues and stacks are used in search algorithms.

How to measure execution time.

How to count visited nodes.

How to compare algorithm performance using actual results.

5. Declaration

I used AI assistance for learning, coding support, and documentation. I reviewed the generated content and take responsibility for understanding and submitting the work.
